+++ b/audit/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,122 @@
+# Strict IW7 consumption audit — source candidate
+
+This separate Windows/MSVC executable reads one original `.gscbin` from binary
+stdin. It emits a JSON witness only after strict container, zlib, disassembler and
+local-function-resolution checks succeed. It does not compile GSC, write assets,
+run a game or establish dependency closure. **Native compilation and execution
+are pending resource admission. No successful native witness exists yet.**
+
+The source baseline is xensik/gsc-tool
+`3300e430d1efef00e54c66a8bd416e18a2a9882a`. This checkout was cloned from the
+already retained local repository without hard links or recursive submodules.
+The shared source was not edited. Publication belongs to the coordinator's private
+tooling workflow; the only configured remote is the local source repository and
+local `push.default=nothing` prevents an implicit push.
+
+## Decoder contract
+
+- The historical `disassemble()` API remains available. The dedicated audit calls
+  `disassemble_strict()` with bounded readers and IW7 PC tables.
+- The first byte must be the table's `OP_End`. Every function has a positive
+  declared length within the remaining bytecode. Every instruction must fit its
+  function, including variable-size instructions and the final function.
+- Both final cursors must equal their full buffer lengths. There is no guessed
+  padding, ignored suffix, implicit terminator repair or relaxed fallback.
+- Strict C strings require a NUL within remaining bytes. Invalid forward/reverse
+  seeks, absolute positions and alignments throw. Existing unknown/unhandled
+  opcode refusals and unresolved local-function refusals remain.
+- The three-byte integer reader now reads exactly three bytes in either mode;
+  its values are preserved while its former four-byte overread is removed.
+- The container uses exact declared lengths. The compressed stream must reach
+  `Z_STREAM_END`, consume all compressed bytes and produce exactly the declared
+  stack size. Concatenated streams and added data are refused.
+- An empty assembler shape is legitimate only as one initial `OP_End`, an empty
+  decompressed stack and no functions. Arbitrary extra bytes are not padding.
+
+Limits are 8 MiB of input and 16 MiB of decompressed stack; these are refusal
+limits, not a compatibility guarantee for all retail scripts. Parsing every
+instruction proves structural consumption under these pinned tables, not engine
+acceptance, runtime semantics or the completeness of the reverse-engineered tables.
+
+## Evidence and identity
+
+`audit/prepare.py` requires a clean committed checkout and generates an ignored
+header plus source manifest. It records the source revision, a canonical digest
+of tracked source files, a separate digest of the IW7 tables and opcode sizing/
+name definitions, and the expected zlib gitlink. It performs no build.
+
+The native witness `iw7.gsc-consumption-native/1` contains hashes and lengths of
+the exact input read from stdin, decoded bytecode, decoded stack and emitted
+assembly; final cursors; contiguous consumption records for each function; and
+the source/table identity compiled into the executable. SHA256 uses Windows
+BCrypt. Assembly is returned as hex to avoid altering its exact bytes in JSON.
+The witness is a measurement by an explicitly pinned tool, not a signature.
+
+The SDK wrapper `sdk/modding/audit_gsc_consumption.py` independently checks framing
+and decompression, passes those same original bytes through stdin, requires
+caller-supplied source/table/revision and executable pins, and hashes the tool
+before and after execution. It validates all witness hashes, cursors, per-function
+partitions and assembly bytes. The executable hash is bound by the wrapper;
+the native decoder binds the bytes it actually read. Consumers must trust the
+reviewed build-to-executable pin, not a self-reported revision on its own.
+
+The wrapper deliberately keeps external dependency absence, asset closure,
+runtime readiness and owner acceptance false. A separate complete import analysis
+may later use the bound assembly; no existing Creator/Recipient gate is changed.
+
+## Prepared tests and current evidence
+
+Nine pure SDK tests pass using synthetic framing and mocked process results.
+They cover input/tool/source/table/assembly binding, both cursor requirements,
+function partitions, compressed/container suffixes, duplicate JSON fields, native
+failure handling and replacement of the executable during an audit. They do not
+execute C++ or establish a real successful witness.
+
+`reader_tests.cpp` is prepared for native reader bounds, NUL, seek/align, exact
+three-byte reads and historical-seek compatibility. `test_native.py` has ten
+native test methods covering valid minimal/string/multiple-function inputs,
+token-encoded external calls, truncation, added bytes in both buffers, zlib
+suffixes, unknown/initial opcodes, last-function sizes and missing NULs.
+These native tests have **not run**. No game or native tool was started.
+
+## Admission and build plan
+
+1. Coordinator releases the active MaterialC workload, fetches the private
+   project origin and rereads current `origin/main:docs/RESOURCE-WORKFLOW.md`.
+   Use its reviewed `Invoke-IW7ResourceJob`, `Kind Build`, **4 GiB physical /
+   6 GiB commit**, one MSBuild node, `/MP` disabled and BelowNormal priority.
+   Keep configuration, compilation and native tests in that admitted synchronous
+   job; preserve diagnostics on failure and release only after children exit.
+2. Verify this source commit and cleanliness. Initialize only the pinned zlib
+   dependency from the existing local source, without network or SDK/game copies.
+   Require `51b7f2abdade71cd9bb0e7a373ef2610ec6f9daf` and a clean checkout.
+   Do not initialize cxxopts: this dedicated target does not use it. Expected
+   extra source/dependency storage is about 10 MiB (existing zlib checkout
+   4,468,081 bytes plus 5,343 KiB Git pack), within the 128 MiB preparation budget.
+3. Generate a fresh ignored identity directory with `python -B audit/prepare.py`.
+   Record its manifest, the source commit, dependency commit and installed compiler
+   and CMake versions. CMake is already available with the local VS 2022 Build
+   Tools; no installation was performed. Set a separate **2 GiB build-output
+   disk allowance**, measured during execution; the 128 MiB limit covers source
+   preparation, not build outputs. Stop and report if that allowance is insufficient.
+4. Configure `audit/CMakeLists.txt` with VS 2022, x64, the generated identity
+   directory and an ignored `build/audit-native` output directory. Build Release
+   with `--parallel 1 -- /m:1 /nr:false /p:MultiProcessorCompilation=false`.
+   This compiles GSC core plus IW7 tables, utils and zlib, excluding ARC, other
+   engine tables and the historical CLI. Exact build/link compatibility is pending.
+5. Run CTest's reader test, then `python -B audit/test_native.py --tool TOOL -v`.
+   Only if those pass, run the pinned SDK wrapper on the already retained Beacon
+   variant and original negative control. A complete-consumption refusal is a
+   result to investigate; never relax suffix or function checks to obtain success.
+   Verify all source/dependency hashes again, hash the executable, retain exact
+   command/exit/measurement evidence and finish the coordinator's private review.
+
+Illustrative commands, to execute only inside the admitted job after step 2:
+
+```text
+python -B audit/prepare.py --output build/identity-reviewed
+cmake -S audit -B build/audit-native -G "Visual Studio 17 2022" -A x64 -DAUDIT_IDENTITY_DIR=ABSOLUTE_IDENTITY_DIRECTORY
+cmake --build build/audit-native --config Release --parallel 1 -- /m:1 /nr:false /p:MultiProcessorCompilation=false
+ctest --test-dir build/audit-native -C Release --output-on-failure
+python -B audit/test_native.py --tool build/audit-native/Release/iw7-gsc-audit.exe -v
+```
diff --git a/audit/main.cpp b/audit/main.cpp
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..ec48d3cc993e6d02fbb77a3f65c343b98b472851
--- /dev/null
+++ b/audit/main.cpp
@@ -0,0 +1,139 @@
+// Dedicated IW7 PC structural audit. GPLv3; see ../LICENSE.
+#define NOMINMAX
+#define WIN32_LEAN_AND_MEAN
+#include <windows.h>
+#include <bcrypt.h>
+#include <io.h>
+#include <fcntl.h>
+#include "xsk/gsc/engine/iw7.hpp"
+#include "zlib.h"
+#include "audit_identity.hpp"
+
+namespace
+{
+using namespace xsk;
+constexpr usize input_limit = 8 * 1024 * 1024;
+constexpr usize stack_limit = 16 * 1024 * 1024;
+
+auto hex(u8 const* data, usize size) -> std::string
+{
+    static constexpr char digits[] = "0123456789abcdef";
+    std::string result;
+    result.reserve(size * 2);
+    for (usize i = 0; i < size; ++i)
+    {
+        result.push_back(digits[data[i] >> 4]);
+        result.push_back(digits[data[i] & 15]);
+    }
+    return result;
+}
+
+auto sha256(std::vector<u8> const& data) -> std::string
+{
+    BCRYPT_ALG_HANDLE algorithm = nullptr;
+    if (BCryptOpenAlgorithmProvider(&algorithm, BCRYPT_SHA256_ALGORITHM, nullptr, 0) < 0)
+        throw std::runtime_error("SHA256 provider failed");
+    std::array<u8, 32> digest{};
+    auto status = BCryptHash(algorithm, nullptr, 0, const_cast<u8*>(data.data()),
+        static_cast<ULONG>(data.size()), digest.data(), static_cast<ULONG>(digest.size()));
+    BCryptCloseAlgorithmProvider(algorithm, 0);
+    if (status < 0) throw std::runtime_error("SHA256 failed");
+    return hex(digest.data(), digest.size());
+}
+
+auto read_input() -> std::vector<u8>
+{
+    if (_setmode(_fileno(stdin), _O_BINARY) == -1)
+        throw std::runtime_error("binary stdin unavailable");
+    std::vector<u8> data;
+    std::array<char, 8192> block{};
+    while (std::cin)
+    {
+        std::cin.read(block.data(), block.size());
+        auto count = static_cast<usize>(std::cin.gcount());
+        if (count > input_limit - data.size()) throw std::runtime_error("input exceeds audit limit");
+        data.insert(data.end(), block.data(), block.data() + count);
+    }
+    if (!std::cin.eof()) throw std::runtime_error("stdin read failed");
+    return data;
+}
+
+auto unpack(std::vector<u8> const& data) -> std::pair<std::vector<u8>, std::vector<u8>>
+{
+    if (data.size() < 16 || std::memcmp(data.data(), "GSC\0", 4))
+        throw std::runtime_error("expected GSC container");
+    utils::reader input{ data.data(), data.size(), false, true };
+    input.seek(4);
+    auto compressed_size = input.read<u32>();
+    auto stack_size = input.read<u32>();
+    auto code_size = input.read<u32>();
+    if (!compressed_size || !code_size || code_size > input_limit || stack_size > stack_limit ||
+        static_cast<usize>(compressed_size) + code_size != data.size() - 16)
+        throw std::runtime_error("invalid container lengths or trailing container bytes");
+    // One spare byte distinguishes declared size from an overproducing stream.
+    std::vector<u8> stack(static_cast<usize>(stack_size) + 1);
+    z_stream stream{};
+    stream.next_in = const_cast<u8*>(data.data() + 16);
+    stream.avail_in = compressed_size;
+    stream.next_out = stack.data();
+    stream.avail_out = static_cast<uInt>(stack.size());
+    if (inflateInit(&stream) != Z_OK) throw std::runtime_error("inflate initialization failed");
+    auto result = inflate(&stream, Z_FINISH);
+    auto consumed = stream.total_in;
+    auto produced = stream.total_out;
+    inflateEnd(&stream);
+    if (result != Z_STREAM_END || consumed != compressed_size || produced != stack_size)
+        throw std::runtime_error("compressed stack is truncated, trailing or size mismatched");
+    stack.resize(stack_size);
+    return { std::vector<u8>(data.begin() + 16 + compressed_size, data.end()), std::move(stack) };
+}
+
+auto audit(std::vector<u8> const& input) -> std::string
+{
+    auto [code, stack] = unpack(input);
+    gsc::iw7::context context{ gsc::instance::server };
+    context.init(gsc::build::prod, {});
+    auto [program, consumed] = context.disassembler().disassemble_strict(code, stack);
+    auto assembly = context.printer().print(*program);
+    // Emit only after every decoder check and function resolution succeeded.
+    std::ostringstream out;
+    out << "{\"schema\":\"iw7.gsc-consumption-native/1\",\"engine\":\"iw7-pc\","
+        << "\"source_revision\":\"" << AUDIT_SOURCE_REVISION << "\","
+        << "\"source_sha256\":\"" << AUDIT_SOURCE_SHA256 << "\","
+        << "\"tables_sha256\":\"" << AUDIT_TABLES_SHA256 << "\","
+        << "\"input_bytes\":" << input.size() << ",\"input_sha256\":\"" << sha256(input) << "\","
+        << "\"bytecode_bytes\":" << code.size() << ",\"bytecode_sha256\":\"" << sha256(code) << "\","
+        << "\"stack_bytes\":" << stack.size() << ",\"stack_sha256\":\"" << sha256(stack) << "\","
+        << "\"bytecode_consumed\":" << consumed.bytecode_consumed << ","
+        << "\"stack_consumed\":" << consumed.stack_consumed << ","
+        << "\"initial_op_end_verified\":true,\"complete_consumption_verified\":true,"
+        << "\"functions\":[";
+    for (usize i = 0; i < consumed.functions.size(); ++i)
+    {
+        auto const& f = consumed.functions[i];
+        if (i) out << ',';
+        out << "{\"bytecode_begin\":" << f.bytecode_begin << ",\"declared_bytes\":" << f.declared_bytes
+            << ",\"bytecode_end\":" << f.bytecode_end << ",\"stack_begin\":" << f.stack_begin
+            << ",\"stack_end\":" << f.stack_end << '}';
+    }
+    out << "],\"assembly_bytes\":" << assembly.size() << ",\"assembly_sha256\":\"" << sha256(assembly)
+        << "\",\"assembly_hex\":\"" << hex(assembly.data(), assembly.size()) << "\"}\n";
+    return out.str();
+}
+}
+
+int main(int argc, char** argv)
+{
+    try
+    {
+        if (argc != 2 || std::string_view{ argv[1] } != "--stdin-gscbin")
+            throw std::runtime_error("usage: iw7-gsc-audit --stdin-gscbin < input.gscbin");
+        std::cout << audit(read_input());
+        return 0;
+    }
+    catch (std::exception const& error)
+    {
+        std::cerr << "audit refused: " << error.what() << '\n';
+        return 1;
+    }
+}
